OL,3,GNEWSABomb squad destroys five suspect
OL,4,Aitems on beach
OL,5,
OL,6,FFive suspected explosive items have
OL,7,Fbeen destroyed by a bomb squad.
OL,9,FWhitehaven Coastguard Rescue Team said
OL,10,Fsomeone spotted a "concerning object"
OL,11,Fwhile at Drigg beach on Friday at about
OL,12,F12:00 BST, which triggered a response
OL,13,Ffrom the Explosive Ordnance Disposal
OL,14,F(EOD) unit.
OL,16,FDue to tide times, the EOD team carried
OL,17,Fout a controlled explosion two days
OL,18,Flater on Sunday at 14:20.
OL,20,FA number of artillery shells and mortar
OL,21,Fwere found on the same beach at
OL,22,Fdifferent times during 2025.
OL,23,APub: 07-SepQppppppppppppppppppppppppppp
